# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# Hand-maintained: edit this file directly.
#
# The legacy /docs/api/* paths come from the pre-v2 (betterdocs) structure
# and are still indexed by Google, so each one answers a 301. Old links
# carried both forms, so every path is listed with and without a trailing
# slash.
#
# Most mappings are a mechanical rename:
#
#   /docs/api/teams/<page>    ->  /docs/reference/team/<page>
#   /docs/api/players/<page>  ->  /docs/reference/player/<page>
#   /docs/api/events/<page>   ->  /docs/reference/events/<page>
#   /docs/api/matches/<page>  ->  /docs/reference/matches/<page>
#   /docs/api/series/<page>   ->  /docs/reference/series/<page>
#   /docs/api/news/<page>     ->  /docs/reference/news/<page>
#
# The exceptions are the paths that were renamed rather than moved. These
# are the ones to check when a docs reference page is renamed:
#
#   /docs/api/teams/previous-players  ->  /docs/reference/team/roster
#   /docs/api/players/agent-stats     ->  /docs/reference/player/agents
#   /docs/api/events/list-events      ->  /docs/reference/events/list
#   /docs/api/events/match-summary    ->  /docs/reference/events/matches
#
# Cloudflare Pages validates this file at deploy time, so a malformed rule
# fails the Pages build rather than shipping.

